---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<Layout title="Product" description="How Laissez works: eligibility credentials, rule packs, a policy resolver, atomic settlement and a signed evidence trail." path="product/">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product</p>
      <h1>Five services. One decision before every token moves.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Laissez sits between the systems distributors already run and the registries issuers already run. It does not hold assets, replace a transfer agent or ask anyone to change token standards.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta"><a class="btn brass" href={url('demo/')}>Try the live demo</a><a class="btn" href={url('developers/')}>API overview</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <figure class="arch" aria-label="Architecture: distributor systems call Laissez, which checks credentials and rule packs, then instructs settlement on the issuer's registry and cash rails">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1100 470" role="img">
          <title>Laissez architecture</title>
          <g class="col">
            <text x="20" y="28" class="h">Distributor</text>
            <rect x="20" y="50" width="220" height="70" rx="14" /><text x="40" y="82" class="t">Order management</text><text x="40" y="104" class="s">tickets, suitability</text>
            <rect x="20" y="140" width="220" height="70" rx="14" /><text x="40" y="172" class="t">KYC and onboarding</text><text x="40" y="194" class="s">evidence stays here</text>
            <rect x="20" y="230" width="220" height="70" rx="14" /><text x="40" y="262" class="t">Client wallets</text><text x="40" y="284" class="s">custodial or self-held</text>
          </g>
          <rect x="300" y="40" width="500" height="390" rx="24" class="core" />
          <text x="330" y="78" class="h brass">Laissez</text>
          <g class="svc">
            <rect x="330" y="100" width="210" height="76" rx="14" /><text x="350" y="134" class="t">Eligibility credential</text><text x="350" y="156" class="s">verify once, reuse everywhere</text>
            <rect x="560" y="100" width="210" height="76" rx="14" /><text x="580" y="134" class="t">Rule packs</text><text x="580" y="156" class="s">versioned, counsel-approved</text>
            <rect x="330" y="196" width="440" height="76" rx="14" class="hl" /><text x="350" y="230" class="t">Policy resolver</text><text x="350" y="252" class="s">fund policy, residence law, booking licence, global screens</text>
            <rect x="330" y="292" width="210" height="76" rx="14" /><text x="350" y="326" class="t">Settlement orchestrator</text><text x="350" y="348" class="s">atomic delivery vs payment</text>
            <rect x="560" y="292" width="210" height="76" rx="14" /><text x="580" y="326" class="t">Evidence ledger</text><text x="580" y="348" class="s">signed receipts, hashes</text>
          </g>
          <text x="330" y="404" class="s">Regulatory change agent drafts rule updates; counsel approves before release</text>
          <g class="col">
            <text x="860" y="28" class="h">Issuer and rails</text>
            <rect x="860" y="50" width="220" height="70" rx="14" /><text x="880" y="82" class="t">Identity registry</text><text x="880" y="104" class="s">ERC-3643 trusted claims</text>
            <rect x="860" y="140" width="220" height="70" rx="14" /><text x="880" y="172" class="t">Fund token</text><text x="880" y="194" class="s">issuer’s chain and agent</text>
            <rect x="860" y="230" width="220" height="70" rx="14" /><text x="880" y="262" class="t">Cash leg</text><text x="880" y="284" class="s">USDC, EURC, deposit tokens</text>
            <rect x="860" y="320" width="220" height="70" rx="14" /><text x="880" y="352" class="t">Travel Rule network</text><text x="880" y="374" class="s">IVMS101 messages</text>
          </g>
          <path d="M240 85 H300 M240 175 H300 M240 265 H300" class="link" />
          <path d="M800 85 H860 M800 175 H860 M800 265 H860 M800 355 H860" class="link" />
        </svg>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band light" id="credential">
    <div class="wrap cols-2">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Eligibility credential</p><h2>The investor is verified once. The result travels.</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">A credential records the investor’s legal classification in each jurisdiction that matters to them: a Singapore accredited investor who has opted in, a Hong Kong professional investor, a Swiss professional client. Each classification carries its citation, the evidence reference and an expiry.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Issued by the distributor that performed KYC, under reliance terms the issuer accepts</li>
          <li>Accepted by issuers as a trusted claim in their existing ERC-3643 identity registry</li>
          <li>Renewal is a re-attestation, not a new onboarding</li>
          <li>Holds references and hashes, never the underlying documents</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="resolver">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Policy resolver</p><h2>Four layers, evaluated in order, every time.</h2></div><p class="lede">Every rule that applies must hold. Where two layers test the same jurisdiction, the stricter test binds. The decision names the binding rule and, on a refusal, the fix.</p></div>
      <div class="cols-4">
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Layer 1</span><h4>Credential</h4><p>Is this the investor that was verified, is the credential current, and is there a sanctions match?</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Layer 2</span><h4>Fund policy</h4><p>Where the issuer offers the fund, to which investor classes, minimums, holder caps, lock-ups and accepted settlement assets.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Layer 3</span><h4>Residence law</h4><p>What the investor’s home jurisdiction requires before this kind of fund can be offered to them.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="k">Layer 4</span><h4>Booking licence</h4><p>What the distributor’s licence in the booking location permits, which can be stricter than the investor’s home law.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="states">
        <h3>Holder states</h3>
        <div class="state-row">
          <div class="st"><span class="dot g"></span><h4>Eligible</h4><p>Can subscribe, receive transfers and redeem.</p></div>
          <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="st"><span class="dot b"></span><h4>Redemption-only</h4><p>Status lapsed or the issuer stopped offering in that jurisdiction. Can always exit, cannot add.</p></div>
          <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="st"><span class="dot c"></span><h4>Frozen</h4><p>Sanctions program applies. Units stay in place and compliance is notified.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band light" id="settlement">
    <div class="wrap cols-2">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Settlement orchestrator</p><h2>Delivery versus payment, in one transaction.</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">Once a decision allows an order, Laissez builds the settlement instruction: the cash leg locks, the registry confirms the receiving wallet’s claim, and fund units and cash swap together on the issuer’s chain.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><div><h4>Decision signed</h4><p>The resolver signs the outcome and the rule-pack versions it used.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h4>Cash leg locked</h4><p>USDC, EURC or a bank deposit token moves into the settlement contract.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h4>Registry confirms</h4><p>The issuer’s identity registry accepts Laissez’s claim for the receiving wallet.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h4>Atomic swap</h4><p>Units and cash exchange in the same transaction. If either leg fails, both revert.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="evidence">
    <div class="wrap cols-2">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Evidence ledger and rule governance</p><h2>Every decision can be proven. Every rule has an owner.</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">Receipts record the outcome, the binding rules, the rule-pack versions and a hash of the inputs. Rule packs change only through a two-person release: a regulatory change agent drafts the diff from regulator publications with citations, and counsel approves it.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Only outcome, input hash and rule versions are written on-chain</li>
          <li>Rule changes preview their effect on existing holders before release</li>
          <li>Proposals stay inactive until they become law, such as the UK’s pending client categorisation changes</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a class="text-link" href={url('trust/')}>How we handle data and keys</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .arch { margin: 0; overflow-x: auto; }
  .arch svg { min-width: 760px; width: 100%; }
  .arch rect { fill: var(--night-2); stroke: var(--hair-2); }
  .arch .core { fill: rgba(201, 169, 110, 0.05); stroke: rgba(230, 210, 164, 0.45); }
  .arch .svc rect { fill: var(--night-3); }
  .arch .svc rect.hl { stroke: rgba(230, 210, 164, 0.6); }
  .arch .h { font: 500 15px var(--f-ui); fill: var(--text-3); }
  .arch .h.brass { font: 400 24px var(--f-display); fill: var(--brass-2); }
  .arch .t { font: 500 16px var(--f-ui); fill: var(--text); }
  .arch .s { font: 400 13px var(--f-ui); fill: var(--text-3); }
  .arch .link { stroke: rgba(230, 210, 164, 0.5); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 4 5; fill: none; }
  .states { margin-top: 4.5rem; }
  .states h3 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .state-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 3rem 1fr 3rem 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .st { background: var(--night-2); border: 1px solid var(--hair-2); border-radius: 16px; padding: 1.4rem; height: 100%; }
  .st h4 { margin: 0.6rem 0 0.4rem; }
  .st p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-2); font-size: 0.94rem; }
  .dot { display: block; width: 0.7rem; height: 0.7rem; border-radius: 50%; }
  .dot.g { background: var(--verdigris); } .dot.b { background: var(--brass); } .dot.c { background: var(--coral); }
  .arrow { height: 1px; background: var(--hair-2); position: relative; }
  .arrow::after { content: ''; position: absolute; right: 0; top: -3px; border: solid var(--text-3); border-width: 0 1px 1px 0; width: 6px; height: 6px; transform: rotate(-45deg); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .state-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .arrow { display: none; } }
</style>
